"Review complete. Everything is verified with direct evidence.\n\n## `fmtcsv.py` diff — parsing logic only\n\n```diff\n--- a/fmtcsv.py\n+++ b/fmtcsv.py\n@@ def parse_csv(path):\n-    Uses csv.reader defaults, which keep the exact content of quoted\n-    fields, including leading/trailing whitespace inside quotes.\n+    Uses csv.reader with skipinitialspace so whitespace between a\n+    delimiter and the next field's opening quote doesn't split quoted\n+    fields. The exact content of quoted fields, including\n+    leading/trailing whitespace inside quotes, is preserved.\n     \"\"\"\n     with open(path, newline=\"\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n-        return list(csv.reader(f))\n+        # skipinitialspace ignores whitespace between a delimiter and the next\n+        # field's opening quote, so quoted fields after \", \" stay one field.\n+        return list(csv.reader(f, skipinitialspace=True))\n```\n\nThe diff touches only `parse_csv` — one functional line plus its docstring/comments. `format_summary`, `main`, argument parsing, error codes, and the print loop are byte-for-byte unchanged, so the summary format cannot have drifted. Full transparency: the docstring update itself is new this turn — I spotted the stale \"uses defaults\" wording while reviewing and corrected it; it's documentation only.\n\n## `test_fmtcsv.py` diff — purely additive\n\nOne new fixture (`spaced_delimiter_csv`) and two new tests (`test_parse_csv_quoted_commas_after_spaced_delimiter`, `test_cli_quoted_comma_after_spaced_delimiter`). The diff confirms zero modifications to any existing test.\n\n## Behavioral verification\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| New tests against **pre-fix** code | `2 failed, 10 passed` — they genuinely catch the bug |\n| Full suite on **current** code | `12 passed` |\n| Spaces inside quotes, old vs new A/B on `Alice,\"  padded  \"` | Output **byte-identical**: `['Alice', '  padded  ']` |\n| Summary printing, old vs new | Same code path, unchanged in diff; exact-stdout CLI tests pass |\n\n**Conclusion:** the patch modifies only the parsing logic (`skipinitialspace=True`), adds regression tests, and leaves spaces-inside-quotes handling and summary printing provably untouched."